}

uhCkkL0DkP-CoGx6_Jzsw90KIt-c5iYP-1jHS62w.description:
{
  "outcome": "The skill places detail correctly: most specs live low, on the Small leaves that will be built; a branch's spec is not a restatement of its children but a higher-level view — often a flow or interaction diagram — of how the parts below it fit together. Completion criteria attach wherever they can be evaluated."
}

uhCkktepnjIU5xA_Vc29afoJxdyqP9hbH_GpgU0E.description:
{
  "outcome": "The skill describes how the LLM works a tree in practice: read the live tree for context, propose typed edits that open a draft for the human to review and commit, and never write to the DHT directly. It is the LLM-facing companion to the human-approved draft flow."
}

uhCkk0ZVQBP7RIyxcSZ6Lh5GFTOK5A3yvQlYm2fd.description:
{
  "outcome": "To talk together about nodes — in chat, in proposals, across sessions — humans and LLMs need an unambiguous way to refer to a specific node that survives the tree being rearranged. Positional or semantic labels (\"i3c\", \"branch L\") break the moment the tree changes; the actionHash is stable but not human-usable; the current 6-digit hashCodeId is stable but opaque and derived from the hash. What the right referent is — a stable id, a human-memorable handle, or both, and how it is displayed and resolved — still needs discussion. (No leaf yet: open for decomposition.)"
}
